// addr_field_local.tk -- D104: `&h.n` on a LOCAL object, from OUTSIDE the
// type. `(&h).n` is `ld64(&h + 24)` -- the local's own stack slot plus the
// offset -- and answered 243 against a field worth 42 at `f81e0217`. D97 read
// the same fragment as "the slot's address plus the offset" and missed the
// enclosing `ld64`, which is why its own entry called this a wrong ANSWER
// that sometimes faults rather than a field load past the frame.
//
// The tell the scout measured: this miscompile fires only when exactly ONE
// type in the unit declares the member name. Add a second class declaring
// `n` and the very same program is refused
// `teko: the type of the left side of `.` is not known here: n` instead,
// because the last-resort resolution by NAME (`tk_pend_by_name`) is what the
// row fell through to. Both now answer the message below.
//
// The road that works: `bump(ref h.n)` / `setit(out h.n)`, proved by
// `tests/addr_not_member.tk` and `tests/ref_field_param.tk`.
//
// expect-refuse: teko: the address of a field is not taught yet; pass it as `ref` or `out`: n
// expect-refuse-line: 26
#include "../../lib/rt.tk"

class H { public i64 n; public H() { n = 42; } }

i64 main() {
    H h = new H();
    return ld64(&h.n);
}
